<title>SWITZERLAND: BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP FOUR-MAN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP FOUR-MAN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ST MORITZ, Switzerland 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in</p>
<p>the bobsleigh world championship four-man event after the final</p>
<p>two runs on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Switzerland II (Reto Goetschi/Guido Acklin/Daniel Giger/Beat</p>
<p>Seitz) 4 minutes 08.94 seconds (first run 1:02.27/second run</p>
<p>1:02.28/third run 1:02.38/fourth run 1:02.01)</p>
<p>2. Switzerland III (Christian Reich/Steve Anderhub/Roger Graber</p>
<p>/Thomas Handschin) 4:09.12 (1:02.32/1:02.20/ 1:02.48/1:02.12)</p>
<p>3. Switzerland I (Marcel Rohner/Markus Wasser/Thomas Schreiber/</p>
<p>Roland Tanner) 4:09.26 (1:02.40/1:02.31/ 1:02.40/1:02.15)</p>
<p>4. Germany I (Wolfgang Hoppe/Sven Ruehr/Rene Hannemann/Carsten</p>
<p>Embach) 4:09.38</p>
<p>5. Germany II (Dirk Wiesse/Markus Zimmermann/Christoph Bartsch/</p>
<p>Michael Liekmeier) 4:09.86</p>
<p>6. U.S. I (Brian Shimer/Chip Minton/Randy Jones/Robert Olesen)</p>
<p>4:09.87</p>
<p>7. Britain I (Sean Olsson/Dean Ward/Courtney Rumbolt/Lenny Paul</p>
<p>) 4:10.00</p>
<p>8. France I (Bruno Mingeon/Emanuel Hostache/Eric Le Chanony/Max</p>
<p>Robert) 4:10.46</p>
<p>9. Austria I (Hubert Schosser/Erwin Arnold/Gerd Habermueller/</p>
<p>Martin Schuetzenauer) 4:10.73</p>
<p>10. Canada I (Pierre Lueders/Dave MacEachern/Matt Hindle/Ben</p>
<p>Hindle) 4:10.96</p>
</text>
